It's a combination of the interface and your own fault.  The interface
is separate from the game.  You are still playing the same game
whether you are using tiles or not, just with a different interface. 
Confirmations are also part of the interface.

If anyone ever wrote an interface that prevented typoes, without
preventing anything stupid that is not a typo, it would be vastly
superior.  Everyone would enjoy it more, except for people who just
don't like change.  The primary reason no one writes such an interface
is because it is not possible.

But in the few cases where typos are preventable without preventing
poor decisions, they should be.  If they slow down the game, they can
be made an option.  I think this is such a case.

Games are fun because they test skill, knowlege, judgement, and
possibly a few other things.  Testing typing skill very rarely makes a
game more fun.

And this is coming from someone who has never blown up a bag of
holding, nor YASDed due to a typo. (I've YASDed plenty of times due to
one keystroke worth of poor judgement tho'.)  So I'm not saying this
because I want the game to be easier.  Just more fun.

